  "question": {
    "text": "A concave mirror of focal length $f$ in air is dipped in a liquid of refractive index $\\mu$. Its focal length in the liquid will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mu f$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$f$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{f}{(\\mu-1)}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{f}{\\mu}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Focal length of mirror will not change because focal length of mirror doesn't depend on medium."
